Aerie-Purpose: Give every frame the renderer piece of cosmetic filtering: it inserts the browser's hide rules as a user-origin sheet and relays late class names and ids, so a page cannot remove the hide and late ad containers are hidden (ADR 0005).
Aerie-Upstream-Area: chrome/renderer/chrome_content_renderer_client.cc (ChromeContentRendererClient::RenderFrameCreated), chrome/renderer/BUILD.gn (renderer deps)
Aerie-Kind: hook

One Create() call and one GN dependency. The agent lives in components/aerie_adblock/renderer
(the overlay). It applies only the CSS the browser sends over the two-call interface in
components/aerie_adblock/common/cosmetic.mojom and has no network or filter list code.
See docs/adr/0005-renderer-side-cosmetic-piece.md and docs/adblock.md.

